      "kind": "imprecise",
      "reason": "collections.abc.Hashable checks for a hash method, not that calling it succeeds. A tuple containing an unhashable member can pass isinstance(tag, Hashable), after which set.update can still raise TypeError; if earlier tags were added first, the update can be partial. The described guard is therefore not complete for all composite labels.",
      "claim": "The answer describes the Hashable pre-check as reliably catching invalid tags before set.update, avoiding the lower-level error and partial updates.",
      "questionNumber": 17,
      "questionPart": "answer",
      "questionFingerprint": "3332ca0e84d1bc804cee9d693829cc6e3d4868ed5ab991e71493d1a13e47aa77"
    }
